1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,382
This iron pillar is about

2
00:00:01,455 --> 00:00:03,200
sixteen hundred years old.

3
00:00:03,418 --> 00:00:05,309
And something helped protect it:

4
00:00:05,382 --> 00:00:06,109
rust.

5
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,218
The pillar stands in Delhi, India.

6
00:00:08,655 --> 00:00:09,527
The part above ground

7
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,273
has survived remarkably well.

8
00:00:11,491 --> 00:00:12,218
But that doesn't mean

9
00:00:12,291 --> 00:00:13,746
the iron never rusts.

10
00:00:13,964 --> 00:00:15,709
A dense layer of corrosion products

11
00:00:15,782 --> 00:00:16,946
formed on its surface.

12
00:00:17,164 --> 00:00:18,473
It makes it harder for moisture

13
00:00:18,546 --> 00:00:19,273
to reach the metal

14
00:00:19,346 --> 00:00:20,909
and slows further damage.

15
00:00:21,164 --> 00:00:22,255
Phosphorus in the iron

16
00:00:22,327 --> 00:00:24,036
helps this protective layer form.

17
00:00:24,291 --> 00:00:25,964
The surrounding conditions matter too.

18
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,146
The pillar isn't invincible:

19
00:00:28,291 --> 00:00:29,527
below ground, it has rusted

20
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:30,436
more heavily.

21
00:00:30,691 --> 00:00:32,146
So rust doesn't always

22
00:00:32,218 --> 00:00:33,527
just destroy iron.

23
00:00:33,746 --> 00:00:35,127
Sometimes, it helps protect

24
00:00:35,164 --> 00:00:36,000
the metal underneath.

